<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="92e550f4-bb69-506c-91a6-5ff4efef53af" activityNameId="c52f4bc6-8d52-5665-bf0a-b7fcd25abd88" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, lignite ash, 0% water, to opencast refill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, lignite ash, 0% water, to opencast refill
backfilled waste composition is (in ppm): H2O n.a.;
Synonyms: ashes form lignite incineration disposed as backfill in opencast lignite mines; 
UUID: 48d841f7-2de8-4036-a09a-52bacb6b5405
This module contains only direct emissions from lignite ash used as backfill in opencast lignite mines: short-term emissions (0-100a) and long-term emissions (&gt;100a) both to ground water. E.g. land-use and energy consumption is *not* included.
Location: Ash composition calculated from country-specific coal composition (GR) and technology-specific transfer coefficients in power plant.
Technology: Lignite ash as backfill in lignite opencast mine (together with tailings)
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: country-specific calculation based on literature data 
Extrapolations: Ash composition calculated from coal composition and transfer coefficients in power plant  (cf. ecoinvent coal report Röder 2003). Transfer coefficients in backfill estimated from data of residual material landfills and estimated carbonate phase of lignite ashes
Uncertainty adjustments: uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from generic formula GSD(c) = N*ln(c)+1. Mean long-term emissions are the emissions until the next glacial period occurs (in 60'000a) and the landfill is eroded. Maximal long-term emissions are the complete emissions of all landfilled material (except Cr). Minimal long-term emissions are derived implicitly from the mean and maximal values assuming a lognormal distribution.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_48d841f7-2de8-4036-a09a-52bacb6b5405.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
